1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:12,574
Niramoy — a voice-first pre-screening system I built. This is the patient's experience.

2
00:00:14,174 --> 00:00:20,049
The patient just enters their phone number — no app, no account to create.

3
00:00:21,449 --> 00:00:28,113
A one-time code to sign in — type it, or speak the digits out loud.

4
00:00:29,513 --> 00:00:45,767
The assistant asks aloud and the mic opens by itself — hands-free, nothing to tap.

5
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:58,487
The patient answers naturally in Bangla or Banglish — voice is the primary path.

6
00:00:59,887 --> 00:01:11,741
It reads the answer back and stores the exact words, never edited — the system's first rule.

7
00:01:13,141 --> 00:01:23,381
It asks spoken follow-up questions; the patient answers each one by voice.

8
00:01:24,781 --> 00:01:35,857
Everything is organized into a structured summary — and read back aloud for review.

9
00:01:37,257 --> 00:01:50,434
They submit. Risk and red-flags are assessed in the background — for the doctor, not the patient.

10
00:01:51,834 --> 00:01:57,105
That's the patient's whole experience. Here's what happens next.

11
00:01:58,705 --> 00:02:08,190
A medic verifies the AI's summary against the patient's exact words, and adds vitals.

12
00:02:09,590 --> 00:02:23,127
The doctor leads with safety — a red-flag rule that runs independently of the AI.

13
00:02:24,527 --> 00:02:36,369
The doctor decides and writes a structured EHR document. The system never diagnoses.

14
00:02:37,769 --> 00:02:46,744
The patient speaks, hands-free; the system structures; the doctor decides. Niramoy.

